INGI AGENT-AUTHORED DERIVATIVES LICENSE
Version 0.2 (experimental)

Licensor: INGI Consulting ApS, Denmark
Work:     Roundtripper, as published in this repository

  NOTICE. This is an experimental license. It has not been reviewed by a
  lawyer. It is not a free-software or open-source license: it restricts
  what humans may do with derivatives. The Licensor intends it to bind to
  the fullest extent the law allows; Section 9 states where that extent
  ends.

0. PURPOSE

The Work was produced with AI agents working under the Licensor's
direction. This license lets anyone run and share the Work, lets agents
build on it freely, and keeps derivatives that humans author by hand
with whoever made them.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1  "Work" means the software and accompanying files published under
     this license.

1.2  "Agent" means software that generates code or text from
     instructions, for example a large language model acting through
     tools.

1.3  "Agent Output" means content an Agent generated.

1.4  "Operator" means the natural or legal person on whose behalf an
     Agent runs. An Agent holds no rights and owes no duties under this
     license; whatever an Agent does is done by its Operator.

1.5  "Human-Authored Content" means content whose expression a natural
     person composed, by whatever route: typed or dictated into a file,
     supplied to an Agent for inclusion, drawn, or made by editing Agent
     Output. Agent Output that reproduces or closely follows
     Human-Authored Content supplied to the Agent is Human-Authored
     Content.
     The following are not Human-Authored Content:
       (a) instructions that describe what content should do or achieve
           (requirements, specifications, bug reports, test results,
           review comments) as opposed to supplying its expression;
       (b) choosing among Agent Outputs, or removing whole files or whole
           functions of Agent Output;
       (c) running build tools, tests, version control and publishing
           steps that do not change content.

1.6  "Derived Work" means a work based on the Work in whole or in part: a
     modified version, a translation, a port, or a work that copies the
     Work or parts of it into itself. Packaging is not a Derived Work. A
     work that merely invokes the Work, as a program or as a library,
     without copying its content into itself is not a Derived Work.

1.7  "Packaging" means metadata, build recipes, wrappers, configuration
     and installation scripts that bundle, build or install the Work or a
     Derived Work without altering its content, and the aggregation of
     the Work or a Derived Work with independent works on one medium or
     in one archive.

1.8  "Agent-Authored Derived Work" means a Derived Work in which every
     difference from the Work is Agent Output or a removal under 1.5(b),
     and which contains no Human-Authored Content beyond what the Work
     itself contains.

1.9  "Human-Authored Derived Work" means any other Derived Work.

1.10 "Distribute" means to make a copy available to anyone other than
     You, in source or any other form, by any means, including network
     access. Transfer within one legal person, or between a natural
     person and the devices they use, is not Distribution.

1.11 "You" means the natural or legal person exercising permissions under
     this license, including through an Agent.

2. THE LICENSOR'S RIGHTS

The Licensor holds and licenses every right in the Work the law gives
it: copyright to the extent the Work embodies the Licensor's own creative
choices, including in the selection, arrangement and structure of its
contents; rights in Agent Output that the Agent's provider assigned to
the Licensor; and any other right. This license claims no more than the
law grants. Section 9 states what follows where no such right exists.

3. PERMISSIONS FOR EVERYONE

Subject to Section 4.2, anyone may, for any purpose including commercial
purposes:
  (a) use, run, build, install, study and test the Work and any
      Agent-Authored Derived Work;
  (b) copy and Distribute verbatim copies of either;
  (c) make Packaging for either, by hand or by Agent, and Distribute it
      together with what it packages.
Running the Work is using a tool. Output the Work produces when run is
not a Derived Work, and this license claims nothing in it.

4. AGENT-AUTHORED DERIVED WORKS

4.1  The Licensor grants every Operator a worldwide, royalty-free,
     non-exclusive, perpetual license to make Agent-Authored Derived
     Works through Agents and to use, copy, modify through Agents,
     Distribute, sublicense and sell them.

4.2  Every copy of the Work or of an Agent-Authored Derived Work that You
     Distribute must
       (a) carry this license unchanged, the Licensor's notices, and any
           agent-authored statements it already carries;
       (b) if it is a Derived Work, state prominently that it is
           agent-authored and name the Agents that produced the changes,
           or the Agent products used where the exact models are unknown;
       (c) be Distributed under this license only. A sublicense may add
           no term that conflicts with it.

5. HUMAN-AUTHORED DERIVED WORKS

5.1  You may make a Human-Authored Derived Work and use it only
     internally: a natural person for their own purposes, on the devices
     they use; a legal person within its own organisation, including
     persons working on its behalf under its control.

5.2  You may not Distribute it, sublicense it, sell it, or use it to
     provide a product or service to anyone else, paid or unpaid,
     including by network access.

5.3  Having an Agent reproduce, restate or closely follow its
     Human-Authored Content does not make the result Agent-Authored
     (Section 1.5).

5.4  The only exception to 5.2 is submission to the Licensor under
     Section 6. Any other use requires a separate written license from
     the Licensor.

6. CONTRIBUTIONS

You may submit a Human-Authored Derived Work, or any other content, to
the Licensor for inclusion in the Work. By submitting it You grant the
Licensor a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free license to
use, modify, Distribute and sublicense the submission as part of the Work
under this license or any later version the Licensor publishes, and You
warrant that You may grant this license. Rights the law does not let You
waive are unaffected.

7. WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT RESTRICT

7.1  Rights that applicable law makes non-excludable. In Denmark these
     include a lawful user's right to make a backup copy, to observe,
     study and test the program, and to decompile it for interoperability
     (ophavsretsloven §§ 36-37), and mandatory consumer protection.

7.2  Rights a hosting platform's terms require the Licensor to grant that
     platform's users, such as viewing and forking a public repository on
     GitHub. Those rights stay as the platform defines them and are not
     extended by this license.

7.3  Any right in the Licensor's names or marks, beyond the attribution
     Section 4.2 requires.

8. ACCEPTANCE AND TERMINATION

8.1  The permissions in Section 3 require no acceptance. Nothing other
     than this license permits You to make or Distribute a Derived Work
     where the Work is protected by a right the Licensor holds; by doing
     either, You accept this license.

8.2  Your rights under this license end automatically if You breach it.
     They are restored if the breach is cured within 30 days of first
     notice from the Licensor. Termination of Your rights does not end
     the rights of others who received copies from You and comply with
     this license.

9. HOW FAR THIS LICENSE BINDS

9.1  Where an act is covered by a right the Licensor holds, Sections 3 to
